{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon","id":20034,"title":"Holiday Pantheon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T19:58:07-08:00","id":20034,"title":"Holiday Pantheon?","content":"So I just found out about this game and how apparently you're the children of various pantheons throughout history. I just had an idea for a possible new pantheon involving holiday mascots and spirits. Below I've written the various &quot;gods&quot; and possible abilities / items they might grant to Scions.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Santa Claus</b> (try explaining that one to your mortal father) - Flying Vehicle, Super Speed (as in visiting all the children in one night!), Crafting Skills (like the elves in his workshop), Easier Passage (as in his tubby frame managing to fit down chimneys without getting stuck.), War Deer (like a war horse, except it's an oversize deer...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Easter Bunny</b> (yeah, you're part bunny!) - Hiding Skills (concealing items from those searching for them), Cooking Skills (particularly sweets), Magical Eggs (crack them open to reveal useful items)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cupid</b> (because cherubs need love too) - Magic Bow &amp; Arrows, Influencing Emotions, Personal Flight (via wings, or some such method)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Saint Patrick</b> - Influencing Luck, Influencing Joy (dancing, singing, partying), Brewing Skills, Magic Pot of Gold, Can Travel Across Rainbows<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack O' Lantern</b> (Some kind of living scarecrow, not just an actual pumpkin!) - Influencing Fear, Power of Disguise, Control Over Monsters (to a limited extent),<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack Frost</b> - Freezing Touch, Resistance to Cold, Can Animate Snow / Ice sculptures into Temporary Servants, Weather Control, Frost Breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I left out any holiday mascots, let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-28-2013, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T08:59:21-08:00","id":20209,"title":"","content":"You forgot Saint Patrick's ability to repel snakes and his Fated Color of Green.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T11:08:51-08:00","id":20254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon#post20034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Santa Claus</b> (try explaining that one to your mortal father) - Flying Vehicle, Super Speed (as in visiting all the children in one night!), Crafting Skills (like the elves in his workshop), Easier Passage (as in his tubby frame managing to fit down chimneys without getting stuck.), War Deer (like a war horse, except it's an oversize deer...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Santa Claus has The Way. Once a year he activates The Way and visits every single home in the world simultaneously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:28:51-08:00","id":20291,"title":"","content":"Well, we have the symbols. We can create names for them. Some of the symbols already have names to them these days thanks to the media.<br /> Santa Claus, Rudolph the red-nosed Reindeer, Ms. Claus, Frosty the Snowman, Elven toy makers, Silver Bell, the decorated Tree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T14:00:07-08:00","id":20353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=20291#post20291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have the symbols. We can create names for them. Some of the symbols already have names to them these days thanks to the media.<br /> Santa Claus, Rudolph the red-nosed Reindeer, Ms. Claus, Frosty the Snowman, Elven toy makers, Silver Bell, the decorated Tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're saying the decorated tree might be part of the pantheon, I'm speechless when trying to imagine how that conception looked!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You are the sexiest tree in the forest! Have my babies!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T14:00:27-08:00","id":20354,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> Santa Claus's associated powers, minus PSP:<br /> Epics: Charisma, Perception<br /> Purviews: Animal (Reindeer), Artistry/Industry (if you have such a purview in game), Justice, Psychopomp<br /> Abilities: Art, Awareness, Control, Craft, Empathy, Larceny","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T15:20:54-08:00","id":20394,"title":"","content":"I didn't know there were a pre-set type of powers and abilities, until I found this section and read through some stuff. I was just guessing what each type of holiday god / goddess might grant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/whitewolf/index.php?title=Character_Creation_%28Scion%29\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiki.white-wolf.com/whitewolf...on_%28Scion%29</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Easter Bunny:</b><br /> Epics: Perception, Dexterity<br /> Purview: Animal (bunny), Fertility, Sun, Health<br /> Abilities: Animal Ken, Psychopomp, Art, Stealth, Athletics, Awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack O' Lantern:</b><br /> Epics: Appearance, Manipulation<br /> Purview: Darkness, Fire, Illusion, Moon<br /> Abilities: Occult, Stealth, Empathy, Integrity, Animal Ken (i.e bats, cats, wolves, and other beasts associated with Halloween), Fortitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T16:17:46-08:00","id":20419,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=20353#post20353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're saying the decorated tree might be part of the pantheon, I'm speechless when trying to imagine how that conception looked!<br /> &quot;You are the sexiest tree in the forest! Have my babies!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Um..no. This is why I mention them as symbols.<br /> <br /> And this is where our imagination comes into play.<br /> <br /> The holiday tree could be a symbol for either a dryad or a &quot;druid&quot; that assumed the symbol ages ago. The applications of symbols are endless when creating deities. Especially seeing as how often the symbol becomes inseparable from the deity him/herself.<br /> <br /> All can be generalized under the heading of the associated holiday. It's kind of elemental in its own way. Santa Claus has evolved to become an elemental of Christmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T22:12:33-08:00","id":21450,"title":"","content":"Alright, I believe I wrote this up fairly well (still not too sure about St. Patrick, so I left him out). How do you (the more experienced players) think it measures up?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Santa Claus:</b><br /> <br /> AKA: Saint Nick, Saint Nicholas, Santa, Tiny Tim<br /> <br /> Santa Claus may be associated with a Christian holiday, but he has garnered enough support and love from the people of the modern world to become a God in his own right. His true god form is exactly what you imagine him to be, the fat, bearded man in a red suit. However, his mortal disguises are far less cheerful and happy to look at. He has been known to appear as an emaciated beggar, a terrified and starving child, or even a rock bottom drug addict. These disguises are actually his own way of testing the compassion and generosity of mortals, and those who show kindness and mercy upon him in these forms are known to receive tremendous rewards in return. Those who take advantage of him in these forms meet terrible consequences for their lack of humanity. Santa Claus has become the chief god of the Holiday pantheon simply because of how much Legend he has amassed. You can even find people setting up Christmas decorations several months before December even arrives! Santa Claus has a strong sense of justice and believes that the good should be rewarded and the evil should be punished. He using his Psychopomp powers to keep tabs on the moral bearings of nearly all the people of the world, categorizing them into the sections Nice (good) and Naughty (evil). Every year on his associated holiday, he delivers reward and punishment to the mortals depending upon which side of the list he attributes them. Children simply get away with coal stuffed into their presents, but older offenders who do not have the naivete of youth to excuse their actions are stricken with more severe punishment. Their homes might get broken into, they may lose their job (and Christmas bonuses), or the gifts that they have been wanting all year may be sold out or recalled due to some kind of defect. Conversely, those who adhere to the Nice list may experience the opposite, citing tales about Christmas Miracles and increasing Santa's Legend accordingly.<br /> <br /> Despite being a married God (Husband of Mrs. Claus), Santa has sired the occasional Scion with mortals in the past. Often, these Scions become famous characters from holiday stories who accrue Legend by the constant retelling of their stories throughout the ages Many of these Scions were conceived with kindhearted women who showed mercy on one of his tragic mortal disguises, after he took on a more appropriate form, of course. Scions of Santa Claus often share his belief in justice, occasionally to a fault. As Heroes, they are known to become vigilantes, using their powers to deliver punishment upon the wicked while defending the innocent from those who would do them harm. Oddly, his Scions don't seem to have any sort of uniform traits or characteristics in their appearance whether before or after their ascension. Famous Scions of Santa Claus who have achieved divinity include the Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present, and Future, Rudolph the Red-nose Reindeer (please don't ask!), and Frosty the Snowman (the mechanics for his conception are equally puzzling).<br /> <br /> Epics: Charisma, Perception<br /> Purviews: Animal (Reindeer), Artistry/Industry, Justice, Psychopomp<br /> Abilities: Art, Awareness, Control, Craft, Empathy, Larceny<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Easter Bunny:</b><br /> <br /> AKA: No other Aliases<br /> <br /> The Easter Bunny was originally a pagan fertility goddess, but later became the symbol of a Christian holiday beloved by children everywhere. Now she has become the goddess of youth and artistry, while still retaining some level connection to Fertility, even if now Cupid has become more iconic with that role. In her true form, she resembles a pink, anthropomorphic bunny the size of a human woman. She is almost entirely naked save for colorful ribbons and sashes she drapes across her form in teasing, erotic displays. While in the mortal world, however, her disguises are usually more modest in their dress code and less immediately recognizable than a giant pink bunny. She has posed as a health instructor and a pregnancy coach in order to help mortal women through term, and help keep men in healthy breeding condition. She has also been an elementary school teacher, encouraging children to express their artistic side with brilliant, colorful paintings and constructions. When she is feeling in a particular lecherous mood, however, she has posed as a playboy bunny, which is where the bulk of her Scions are conceived.<br /> <br /> Her Scions are often just as colorful and flamboyant as the holiday their mother represents. They tend to have ecstatic and cheerful personalities with a love for art. Often being referred to as children at heart, their personality always seems youthful regardless of their apparent age. Even those who advance to an elderly status can still be found playing games with young children and telling them exciting stories from their lives. They love jokes, harmless pranks, and nearly all manner of games be they physical or video in nature. This cheery disposition helps keep the Scions in good spirits even in dire circumstances, but their childish characteristics generally aggravates their fellow gods when a situation calls for absolute focus and seriousness. Upon ascending to the Overworld, many of her Scions undergo a transformation into some manner of bunny-human hybrid. The exact level of how closely they resemble a bunny or a human differs according to the individual, but whatever the case may be, they often need to don human disguises when returning to the mortal world.<br /> <br /> Epics: Perception, Dexterity<br /> Purview: Animal (bunny), Fertility, Sun, Health<br /> Abilities: Animal Ken, Psychopomp, Art, Stealth, Athletics, Awareness<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack O' Lantern:</b><br /> <br /> AKA: Pumpkin King, The Great Pumpkin, Skeleton Jack<br /> <br /> The master of terror and king of the pumpkin patch. Jack O' Lantern is the god of Halloween and believes that scaring people can be fun as well as malicious. He is the God of the Underworld in the Holiday pantheon, because quite frankly he's the only one who's actually suited to it's environment. When he is in the mortal world, he takes on forms that are both entertaining and terrifying to those who look upon him. His true divine form is a living scarecrow with a carved pumpkin for a head which spews flames from it's eyes and mouth when he is angry.. When in the mortal world, he disguises himself as a pumpkin farmer, a costume shop owner, or a haunted theme park manager. He has a strong connection with animals that are associated with fear, especially nocturnal ones. Among some of his most favorite pets include ravens, bats, rats, wolves, and spiders. Jack O' Lantern's Scions often have a rebellious nature but are good natured at heart.<br /> <br /> They are commonly dare devils who live for the thrill and excitement of a good adrenaline rush, and try to convince their friends to join in on the action. They can be remarkably courageous, which pays off in the fight against the Titans and their spawn, but can at times be a drawback as well when they don't pause to think about the consequences of their headstrong actions. Curiously enough, when his Scions finally ascend to the Overworld, their godly forms reflect the appearance of various monsters from all corners of the human imagination (Goblins, Vampires, Werewolves, Witches, Demons, Zombies, and so on). Perhaps this has something to do with their father's holiday involving that mortals dress up like monsters, or it can be an aspect of their father's love for terror. Whatever the case may be, his Scions often have to disguise themselves in human forms to walk openly among the mortal population after their ascension.<br /> <br /> <br /> Epics: Appearance, Manipulation<br /> Purview: Darkness, Fire, Illusion, Moon<br /> Abilities: Occult, Stealth, Empathy, Integrity, Animal Ken, Fortitude<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jack Frost:</b><br /> <br /> AKA: Old Man Winter,<br /> <br /> The prince of winter, at least in this particular Pantheon. Jack Frost has become the God of Seasons for the Holiday Pantheon, but the season he is most well known for (and most attached to) is winter. To a certain extend, he is also recognized as a God of Death, due to the effects that his ice and snow has upon the environment. Every year, he blankets the world with ice and snow causing plants and animals to hibernate for the season, before later melting it for new life to grow and emerge into the world. When he is in a good mood, Jack's work can become artistically beautiful and even romantic to some mortals. When he is angry, however, tragic accidents have been known to occur such as harsh blizzards, slippery roads, falling icicles, thin ice on a skating pond, and travelers getting lost in the wilderness. Jack's true divine form resembles a blue skinned, elf-like man with pointed ears nose, and chin. His body hair is made of living ice crystals and he dresses in a blue and white tunic with pointy tipped shoes. When in his mortal disguises, he has appeared various workers associated with winter, including a hockey coach, an ice road trucker, and even a lumberjack! He is seen as having white hair and a goatee no matter what disguise he takes.<br /> <br /> Scions of Jack Frost are natural survivors who quickly adapt to harsh climates and environments. During the winter time where the terrain becomes rough and slippery, and crops become very difficult to grow, the Scions consider such a time of the year to be the perfect training ground. They will venture out into the wilderness for days or perhaps weeks at a time, learning how to survive under the extreme conditions before returning back to civilization stronger and wiser than before. Some have even chosen to climb icy mountains, or work in ski lodges as survival guides and rescue workers. When the time comes for them to ascend and do battle against the Titans, the Scions of Jack Frost are often capable of composing themselves under extreme stress that other Gods might not have the experience to deal with. Scions of Jack Frost are commonly born with albino traits, inheriting naturally white hair and pale skin tones.<br /> <br /> Epics: Stamina, Strength<br /> <br /> Purview: Frost, Animal (Penguin), Animal (Polar Bear), Psychopomp, Death<br /> <br /> Abilities: Survival, Fortitude, Craft, Animal Ken, Awareness, Art<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cupid:</b><br /> <br /> AKA: St. Valentine, Cherub, The Matchmaker<br /> <br /> The angel of love, Cupid is renowned for his match making talents. He has become the Holiday God of Love, much to the resentment of the Easter Bunny. When in the mortal world, his common disguises include the form of youthful individuals between the ages of 3 to 21 years of age. These forms are usually white males with curly blond hair and bright blue eyes and with very handsome features. He primarily chooses to remain undetected by the public and work from the sidelines to coax mortals into forming relationships with each other. Similarly, his Scions also tend to be talented in pulling strings from the sidelines. They are planners, visionaries, and manipulators who take pleasure in watching a well crafted plan come together, as opposed to rushing through things with a grandiose display. This has had the effect of them finding it more difficult to earn Legend than most other Scions, but the children of Cupid know that these things shouldn't be rushed. Too many relationships end in disaster because those involved didn't think things through ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Scions of Cupid tend to be friendly and good natured individuals. They have a habit of making friends wherever they go. They are also known for being very protective of such connections, using their father's divine power to defend others from harm and keep a watch over them. This protection is often a representation of their love for others, and even when they ascend to the Overworld, they still pop back into the mortal world from time to time in order to check up on those they left behind.<br /> <br /> Epics: Charisma, Manipulation<br /> <br /> Purview: Fertility, Psychopomp, Animal (Dove), Guardian<br /> <br /> Abilities: Empathy, Art, Marksmanship, Investigation, Stealth, Animal Ken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Added some more nicknames that I could think of for them. 12-02-2013, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T14:32:17-08:00","id":21891,"title":"","content":"I was hoping for more feedback on the idea to see if there was anything I should reconsider. But I got a +1 like, so I guess I did something right. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:43:41-08:00","id":21935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=21891#post21891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping for more feedback on the idea to see if there was anything I should reconsider. But I got a +1 like, so I guess I did something right. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that I would make these sorts of characters as Spirits of Nature and of the Land (Scion: Ragnar\u00f6k, page 115-118) as they fit the description (possibly with the exception of Cupid, but I'm not sure), so much that Jack Frost is listed in page 116 and 117.<br /> <br /> But this isn't the comment that you are looking for. For a Pantheon: 5 Gods aren't enough, they lack unity and a PSP. After that you need a Underworld, a Godrealm and a opposing Greater Titan.<br /> <br /> The lack of unity is the main problem for me, it was the same problem for why I didn't like the WWII Pantheons, mainly the Allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T18:01:05-08:00","id":22018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=21935#post21935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that I would make these sorts of characters as Spirits of Nature and of the Land (Scion: Ragnar\u00f6k, page 115-118) as they fit the description (possibly with the exception of Cupid, but I'm not sure), so much that Jack Frost is listed in page 116 and 117.<br /> <br /> But this isn't the comment that you are looking for. For a Pantheon: 5 Gods aren't enough, they lack unity and a PSP. After that you need a Underworld, a Godrealm and a opposing Greater Titan.<br /> <br /> The lack of unity is the main problem for me, it was the same problem for why I didn't like the WWII Pantheons, mainly the Allies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Like I said, I haven't read any of the books yet and only recently found out about the game, so all of this is still new to me. I was trying to think of an underworld / god realm, but it was hard to do one for holidays. Maybe a Nightmare Before Christmas theme where it's separated into multiple territories devoted to a particular holiday?<br /> <br /> <br /> How many gods would you say is necessary to construct a working Pantheon? I've noticed the existing ones have quite a hefty amount, but others have even fewer than the ones I gave. The Soviet, British, French, and the Anuna Pantheons only had 3 members each, so I thought 5 was fairly decent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T18:29:14-08:00","id":22042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=22018#post22018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Like I said, I haven't read any of the books yet and only recently found out about the game, so all of this is still new to me. I was trying to think of an underworld / god realm, but it was hard to do one for holidays. Maybe a Nightmare Before Christmas theme where it's separated into multiple territories devoted to a particular holiday?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the problem with trying to force disconnected myths to live together. You can go the Nightmare Before Christmas, but it will feel disconnected as it is on the movie (since that was the intention), but most likely these wont be the characters from the popular culture that most know.<br /> <br /> For a Fan Pantheon try to pick a coercive theme, like mythology from a game, real mythology... or fabricate your own mythology like the example of the Atlantean Pantheon from Scion: Demigod (a lot of people don't like it because it is fake, but either way is a good experience to make your own).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=22018#post22018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many gods would you say is necessary to construct a working Pantheon? I've noticed the existing ones have quite a hefty amount, but others have even fewer than the ones I gave. The Soviet, British, French, and the Anuna Pantheons only had 3 members each, so I thought 5 was fairly decent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Soviet, The British and The French have fewer because they were written to form the Allied Pantheon, which in my opinion shouldn't be used as a reference for a Pantheon. The Anuna are only mentioned in the Adventure part of Scion: God and don't have a full write up, everything else about them is fan made.<br /> <br /> The number of Gods is an arbitrary number due to the necessities of the Pantheon, namely a God of Death, a God of the Sun, a God of the Moon, a God of Harvest, God of War... common themes that are recurrent in myth. I would say 7 or 8 as a bare minimum or whatever is the number of Gods of the Atzl\u00e1nti have.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do note that if you are doing this for fun, nothing of this matters. Doing a fill write up is time consuming and hard work. <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/whitewolf/index.php?title=Downloadable_Content\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a list of fan work that is fairly complete in its approach.</a> Pick one you like (pick mine, the Yazatas, I like them, but failing that pick the Atua).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 12-02-2013, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T19:10:44-08:00","id":22060,"title":"","content":"Ah, so in order to make a working pantheon, I should come up with deities for all of the themes that are have important influence on everyday life before focusing on anything lesser? Makes sense, I guess. The followers would want an explanation for why such events / themes have a strong presence in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T12:52:40-08:00","id":25307,"title":"","content":"This seems to be a very USA oriented Pantheon. There are many holidays from Holi to Tet that could be included. Even sticking to a strictly USA/Western Culture point of view you could add in the Glorious Fourth, the Queen of May, Columbus Day, and other figures.<br /> <br /> Please decide how wide a potion of the planet you're getting your holidays from.<br /> <br /> As to virtues and PSP Expression pops out as a key virtue for this group. Given the seasonal themes I'd also look into Order and or Harmony. The PSP should involve time, memory, and comunity. These are vital to holidays, and Memory and comunity are both hallowed and strengthen by observing holidays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T14:19:19-08:00","id":26032,"title":"","content":"Actually. Brom wrote a book called Kraumpus The Yule Lord. In it, he implied that Kraumpus was the son of Hel, which made him part of Loki's bloodline. Santa Claus was the resurrected Baldr that took on the mantle somewhat after the desolation that was Ragnarok happened. Check it out. It may give people ideas of how Christianity altered some aspects of the pantheons affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T22:18:48-08:00","id":26304,"title":"","content":"I like them, not necessarily for a full-on pantheon, but for a group of lesser deities that PC's might run into... or even if you asked your players to come up with holiday-themed characters, that would be cool too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T04:48:40-08:00","id":27121,"title":"","content":"Given that Holidays define sacred time in the same way temples define sacred space each pantheon would have it's own deity patrons of the Holidays. Example: Joyboy is a spirit of West African origin who is the living embodiment of festival. He seeks to keep the people strong through comunal celebrations. Strong enough to survive oppression, and strong enough to fight back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T07:54:07-08:00","id":30419,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://fc08.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2010/348/e/2/silent_night_rumble_by_hbdesign-d34uqyp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Santa Claus<br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities: Control, Command, Craft, Fotitude, Animal ken, Integrity<br /> <br /> <br /> Epic Attributes: Stamina ,Appearance, Strength, Charisma<br /> <br /> <br /> Purviews: Animal (Reindeer), Frost, Magic ,Mystery, Psychopomp, Sky<br /> <br /> <br /> Rivals: Easter Bunny<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relics: Santas Dress ( Frost Immunity,Frost Purview) ,<br /> <br /> santa's sleigh ( can compresse Time ,say 24 for santa will become 1 hour of real time; also enables the Psychopomp and Sky Purview ) ,<br /> <br /> Glasses ( Magic , Mystery)<br /> <br /> Santas Bag of Toys ( made of a patch of Skin from Cthulhu this Relic has an Infinite Space inside where Santa can store up as much as he want inside of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","user":"DeadGuy","date":". 12-15-2013, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T12:34:43-08:00","id":30524,"title":"","content":"As interesting and dare I say, cool, as that image may be, it kinda doesn't feel very Christmas..ish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T01:53:50-08:00","id":30845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Santas Bag of Toys ( made of a patch of Skin from Cthulhu this Relic has an Infinite Space inside where Santa can store up as much as he want inside of it. </div> </div> </div><b>From Cthulhu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-16-2013, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T06:57:44-08:00","id":30943,"title":"","content":"Hhmmm, I'm trying to make a write-up on T\u00e1o Qu\u00e2n, the Vietnamese Kitchens God, except that he is originally one single guy in Chinese Taoist but split into 2 guys and 1 girl (it's a triangle love kind of thing) when the Vietnamese people adopted his myth. Should I try to explain his paradox origin or just choose one origin and pretend the other one don't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T11:39:12-08:00","id":40610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20034-holiday-pantheon?p=30943#post30943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hhmmm, I'm trying to make a write-up on T\u00e1o Qu\u00e2n, the Vietnamese Kitchens God, except that he is originally one single guy in Chinese Taoist but split into 2 guys and 1 girl (it's a triangle love kind of thing) when the Vietnamese people adopted his myth. Should I try to explain his paradox origin or just choose one origin and pretend the other one don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods and goddesses often have conflicted backgrounds depending upon when they originated and who assimilates them into their culture. Instead of looking at this as a paradox, I'd view this to be an evolution of the god's story and focus on providing rules for his current form. You can figure out a catalyst (e.g. some sort of bridge) later. Ancient history is cool -- but is it relevant to your game?<br /> <br /> For a holiday-related pantheon, I'd put together a collection of lightbringing gods and goddesses. The sun (or son, if you're Christian) coming back into the world is a big part of how this holiday evolved. Gods like: Mithras, Saturn, Apollo, Ishtar, Marduk, and Osiris. The lightbringers do tend to be male-dominated, though! Wheels turning, calendars changing are also good ones to look at like Janus or the Holly/Oak King and Osiris/Isis myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}